course: dictionary
lesson: 1238
title: Bump: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one is right. Bump is a good example. It can be a noun, a thing like a bump in a road, or a verb, an action like hitting something. «The car hit a bump in the road.» Here the bump is a raised part of the road, because the car hit it.
explain: «I bumped my head on the low shelf.» Bumped is a verb, so something happened by accident. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: "I hit my head on the low shelf" still makes sense, so bump means hit here.
explain: Bump can also be a swelling on your body. «The bump on my head is going purple.» The words head and purple tell you it is a swelling, not a road. When you meet a new meaning, ask yourself what the nearby words are about.
fact: A bump can be a raised round part on a surface, like a bump in a road.
fact: To bump into something is to hit it by accident; to bump into someone is to meet them by chance.
fact: A bump on the head should be told to an adult, especially if you feel sick or dizzy.
fact: The size of a bump does not show how serious the injury is.
fact: Humpback whales have a row of bumps on the front edge of their flippers, which helps them turn tightly.
exercise: «The car hit a bump in the road.» What is a bump here? | A loud party | A swelling on your body | A kind of song | *A raised round part on the road
exercise: «I bumped into Sam at the shop, we had not met for years.» What does bumped into mean here? | Fell over | Hit something by accident | *Met by chance | Shouted loudly
exercise: Mum says, «Tell me if you feel sick, because you bumped your head.» Why does she say this? | Only sore arms need telling | A bump on the head is never worth mentioning | Sick people never bump their heads | *A bump on the head can be serious, so an adult must know
test: «Saying sorry when you hurt or bump someone shows you care about how they feel.» What does bump mean here? | Make a loud noise | Meet someone by chance | *Hit someone by accident | A round raised shape
test: In Chinese, you say duìbuqǐ (sorry) and the other person answers méi guānxi. What does méi guānxi mean? | Goodbye | Sorry | Hello | *Never mind
exam: «Something went bump in the night.» What does bump mean here? | To meet someone by chance | A raised part of a road | *A dull sound of something hitting something | A swelling on the body
